From e4b6c50a0a5511337695951f5828b2c78fc191ec Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 06:21:42 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] A refused auto-continue kickoff drops its marker
 inputs and caps its watcher re-arms

Follow-up to #1905 review nits (t_01a1d37aace2c43f):

- The kickoff sets _auto_continue_attempt/_prompt/_pauses/_killed_jobs and _marker_until_tool for the turn to
  read back; only a started turn pops them. A refused submit (and the dispatch-exception branch) now drops
  them, so a user turn that starts before the re-armed continuation records its own marker, not the paused
  prompt, its attempt count or its at-most-once flag. _marker_until_tool is dropped only when the kickoff set
  it True (the key is shared with user turns).
- Re-arms of the pause watcher are capped at REFUSED_REARM_MAX (6) per pause (session_key, started_at,
  pauses): each re-arm was a fresh watcher with a fresh budget, so a refusal that persists looped every
  ~10-15 s until the marker aged out. An ownership refusal (_turn_owner_refusal, e.g. SESSION_MOVED) never
  re-arms: no watcher waits another owner out.
- Docstring, comment and WARNING no longer claim a 30 s retry: nothing re-polls; the next resume, boot sweep
  or refused-turn timer retries (as after a slot refusal).
- New kickoff-level test through the real admission refusal: the update hold re-taken during the build makes
  prepare_work return None; stage/settle release the claim (no token, no reservation), the watcher re-arms and
  a following user turn's marker is clean.

Proof: the 15 tests in test_update_pause_refused_kickoff{,_admission}.py fail 6 on the tree without the fix
and pass 15 with it; 51 tui_gateway update-pause/auto-continue/prompt/admission/marker files pass 457; all 10
mutants (either drop removed, until_tool pop removed, a key kept, owner check removed, cap removed, cap off by
one, count not per pause, pause id without pauses) are killed.
